          %title Relaxed multicategories
          %h1#relaxed_multicategories Relaxed multicategories
          .maruku_toc
            %ul
              %li
                %a{:href => "#idea"} Idea
              %li
                %a{:href => "#sketch_of_a_definition"} Sketch of a definition
              %li
                %a{:href => "#literature"} Literature
          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            Vertex algebras are intuitively analogues of associative algebras, except that certain singularities come up (in physics terminology this comes from
            = succeed "\u2018s)." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/OPE"} OPE
          %p Relaxed multicategories can be thought of, according to Borcherds, as multicategories in which the morphisms may have some sort of singularity. In the language of pseudotensor categories (a variant of coloured operads) this is studied by Beilinson and Drinfeld. In connection to quantum groups this has been studied by Soibelman.
          %h2#sketch_of_a_definition Sketch of a definition
          %p
            Let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi T
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
            be the free
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monoid"} monoid
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monad"} monad
            on
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Set"} Set
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi T
                    %mo +
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T^+
            the monad induced by the adjunction of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/forgetful+functor"} forgetful functor
            from
            = succeed "-multicategories" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi T
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
            = succeed "-graphs." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi T
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
            = succeed "-multicategory" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi T
                      %mo +
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T^+
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/generalized+multicategory"} generalized multicategory
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi V
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
            %strong relaxed multicategory
            is any
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi V
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/enriched+multicategory"} enriched
            = succeed "-multicategory." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi T
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
          %h2#literature Literature
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Tom+Leinster"}> Tom Leinster
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Generalized enrichment for categories and multicategories
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/math/9901139"} math.QA/9901139
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Yan+Soibelman"}> Yan Soibelman
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Meromorphic tensor categories
                = succeed ";" do
                  %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/q-alg/9709030"} q-alg/9709030
                = succeed "," do
                  %em The meromorphic braided categroy arising in quantum affine algebras
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/math/9901003"} math.QA/9901003
            %li
              %p
                Craig T. Snydal,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Relaxed multi category structure of a global category of rings and modules
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/math/9912075"} math.CT/9912075
            %li
              %p
                Craig T. Snydal,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Equivalence of Borcherds G-vertex algebras and axiomatic vertex algebras
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/math/9904104"} math.QA/9904104
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/A.+A.+Beilinson"}> A. A. Beilinson
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/V.+Drinfeld"} V. Drinfeld
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Chiral Algebras
                = succeed ")." do
                  %a{:href => "http://www.math.uchicago.edu/~mitya/langlands.html"} here
